ement item exceeds the<br>threshold set in the threshold register (wxyTh, wzTh), the INT pin will be<br>pulled high, but the baseline value will not be updated, it is still the value of<br>this measurement when wake-up & Sleep mode is turned on for the first<br>time.<br>The following is an example process for measuring the change in the Z-axis<br>magnetic field:<br>·Set the reference value wakeSel =0, wakeDiff =0<br>·The host writes the wake-up threshold into the threshold register wzTh<br>·The host sends a wake-up & Sleep mode command (0x28) to the chip, and<br>the chip records the current Z-axis magnetic field value (BZ1) as the baseline<br>value|


